      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/xanderai/status/2092498217393152234",
      "text": "*at least* two years for humans to contribute to AI research \ud83d\ude0f \n\nThere is no such thing as a model that can represent a human with a decade of experience working with these objects. \n\nSpiky intelligence (getting better at coding, stagnating at creative writing) due to economic incentives. \n\nThe labs are very brutally economically optimizing for survival. If you\u2019re not the lab with the highest compute footprint then you\u2019ll die.\n\nAt the beginning of 2019 Ilya said we need to train a gigantic generative model on all the data we can and then we need to train it with reinforcement learning.",
