      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/xanderai/status/2092456346163786206",
      "text": "\u201cAstra isn\u2019t widely deployed even inside OpenAI\u201d\n\n\u201cThere might be some forces at play that slow that down but we can\u2019t get into that.\u201d \n\n\u201cI expect labs to allocate less and less compute to inference over time.\u201d \n\nChina:\n2026: mostly smuggled chips\n2027: Domestic fabs come online\n2028: 5-10GW domestic chips\n2029: 50GW\n\nKimi is nowhere near 1GW. Anthropic is 5GW by the end of the year. \n\n$11T capex from 2024 to 2029. 6 of they is cash, 5 of that is debt. \n\n\u201cEvery force is screeching towards centralization.\u201d",
